#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Bot self-audit (2026-10-20): auto-repair health check for the paper bot.

Runs once per invocation (cron / CEO weekly cycle), detects operational
faults, repairs the small safe subset autonomously, and appends one JSON
line to ~/.forex-agent/self_audit.jsonl:
    {ts, ok: [...], repaired: [...], problems: [...]}
Problems it cannot repair land in "problems" for the weekly CEO report.

Detection (read-only):
  1. Every watchdog-supervised daemon alive. The supervised list is
     DERIVED from scripts/forex-watchdog + scripts/forex-daemons at run
     time — never a second hardcoded copy that can drift.
  2. State freshness + parseability: signal bus mtime, spark_seen.json
     mtime, mirror/CEO ledger parse, killswitch state parse, and every
     *ledger*.json in the agent home parses. A freshness check whose
     component is recorded as decommissioned in the registry at
     ~/.forex-agent/decommissioned.json is skipped (reported as an ok
     note, never a problem); removing the registry entry — or setting
     its "decommissioned" flag false — restores the check with no code
     change. A missing/corrupt registry means NO component is treated
     as decommissioned (fail toward alerting, never toward silence).
  3. Latest backup archive younger than 2.5h.
  4. Disk space on the agent home > 1GB free.
  5. DexScreener + RugCheck endpoints reachable (one light GET each).
  6. Toolkit suite (memecoin-toolkit/run_all_tests.sh) passes — run
     AT MOST once per 24h, gated by ~/.forex-agent/toolkit_last_check.json;
     report-only (a failure is unfixable-by-audit, never edited here).
  7. Grad entry flow (2026-11-08): the grad lanes (grad_select /
     tranche / tranche_protect) have taken a new entry recently.
     The 43h drought of 2026-11-06→08 was invisible to this audit
     (traders alive, killswitches unhalted, problems []) because
     entry flow was never checked. Halted lanes and lanes whose
     trader is already dead are skipped — the halt / dead-daemon
     problem already covers those states.

Repairs allowed (each logged): run `bash scripts/forex-watchdog` ONCE
if any daemon is dead; delete a stale (>1h) *.lock file next to the
ledgers ONLY when an flock probe proves no process holds it; rotate a
log file over 50MB (gzip to <name>.1.gz, then truncate).

NEVER: edits code, changes killswitch state, deletes ledgers or state,
restarts healthy daemons, sends Telegram messages.

Usage: bot-self-audit [--dry-run]   (dry-run: findings only, no repairs,
no jsonl append). Exit 0 unless catastrophic.
Free-only: stdlib only.
"""
